jobDescription:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tekion:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Positively disrupting an industry that has not seen any innovation in over 50 years, Tekion has challenged the paradigm with the first and fastest cloud-native automotive platform that includes the revolutionary Automotive Retail Cloud (ARC) for retailers, Automotive Enterprise Cloud (AEC) for manufacturers and other large automotive enterprises and Automotive Partner Cloud (APC) for technology and industry partners. Tekion connects the entire spectrum of the automotive retail ecosystem through one seamless platform. The transformative platform uses cutting-edge technology, big data, machine learning, and AI to seamlessly bring together OEMs, retailers/dealers and consumers. With its highly configurable integration and greater customer engagement capabilities, Tekion is enabling the best automotive retail experiences ever. Tekion employs close to 3,000 people across North America, Asia and Europe.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Job Description&lt;/h3&gt; &lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Staff Product Manager to join the Tekion CRM Product Team. In this role, you will own and evolve core CRM capabilities that power lead management, customer engagement, and sales execution for automotive dealerships at scale. You will work closely with Engineering, Design, Data, GTM, and Customer Success teams to define strategy, drive execution, and deliver measurable business impact. This role is ideal for a product leader who thrives in complex domains, brings strong customer empathy, and can balance long-term platform thinking with near-term execution in a fast-paced Saa S environment.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt; &lt;p&gt;Own Product Strategy &amp;amp; Outcomes&lt;/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end product lifecycle for core Tekion CRM capabilities
- from discovery and definition to launch, adoption, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Define and evolve the product strategy and roadmap, aligned with company goals, customer needs, and platform vision.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt;Drive Business Impact&lt;/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;Drive adoption, penetration, and customer satisfaction for Tekion CRM, with clear accountability for usage, conversion, and customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Partner with GTM and Customer Success teams to ensure features translate into real dealer value.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt;Customer-Centric Product Development&lt;/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of the customer, deeply understanding dealership workflows, sales processes, and lifecycle needs.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Continuously gather and synthesize customer feedback, usage data, and market insights to inform product decisions.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt;Data-Driven Decision Making&lt;/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;Define success metrics and KPIs for your product areas.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Use data to prioritize investments, evaluate trade-offs, and guide iteration post-launch.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership&lt;/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;Lead complex initiatives across Engineering, Design, Data, Marketing, and Customer Success.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Align stakeholders across product verticals to ensure roadmap coherence and platform consistency.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt;Platform &amp;amp; Scale Thinking&lt;/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;Design solutions that scale across dealership sizes, regions, and OEM requirements.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Balance speed with quality, ensuring solutions are configurable, extensible, and sustainable.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt;Mentorship &amp;amp; Product Excellence&lt;/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;Mentor and guide Product Managers, setting a high bar for product thinking, execution, and customer empathy.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Influence product best practices, planning rituals, and decision-making frameworks across the team.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;p&gt;Execution with Velocity&lt;/p&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;Enable teams to move fast without breaking things
- clarifying priorities, managing dependencies, and making informed trade-offs to hit both short-term goals and long-term bets.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;h3&gt;Requirements&lt;/h3&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;8+ years of Product Management experience owning customer-facing Saa S products&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience mentoring or managing Product Managers&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Advanced degree (MBA or Engineering) from a top-tier institution&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Experience leading distributed onshore and offshore teams&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen with ability to operate in complex, multi-stakeholder environments&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Proven track record of driving product adoption and measurable business impact&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with Engineering, Design, Data, and GTM teams&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Strong prioritization skills and ability to align stakeholders across functions&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Hands-on product leader with strong judgment and bias for action&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;End-to-end ownership of the product lifecycle, including post-launch iteration&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Experience building scalable systems and processes&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; &lt;h3&gt;Preferred Skills&lt;/h3&gt; &lt;ul&gt; &lt;li&gt;AI/ ML product management experience&lt;/li&gt; &lt;li&gt;Experience in the automotive retail industry or with dealer/ OEM data.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;hr&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Tekion is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, victim of violence or having a family member who is a victim of violence, the intersectionality of two or more protected categories, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information on our privacy practices, please refer to our Applicant Privacy Notice &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot; href=&quot;https://tekion.com/legal/privacy/applicant-and-candidate-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;re&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tekion:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Positively disrupting an industry that has not seen any innovation in over 50 years, Tekion has challenged the paradigm with the first and fastest cloud-native automotive platform that includes the revolutionary Automotive Retail Cloud (ARC) for retailers, Automotive Enterprise Cloud (AEC) for manufacturers and other large automotive enterprises and Automotive Partner Cloud (APC) for technology and industry partners. Tekion connects the entire spectrum of the automotive retail ecosystem through one seamless platform. The transformative platform uses cutting-edge technology, big data, machine learning, and AI to seamlessly bring together OEMs, retailers/dealers and consumers. With its highly configurable integration and greater customer engagement capabilities, Tekion is enabling the best automotive retail experiences ever. Tekion employs close to 3,000 people across North America, Asia and Europe.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Summary:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;​Leads the design, development, and delivery of complex software systems across Tekion’s platform. Balances hands-on development with technical leadership, mentoring, and cross-functional collaboration to drive impactful outcomes and advance engineering best practices. ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties &amp;amp;

RESPONSIBILITIES:
&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• ​Leads end-to-end technical execution for major projects, from design through deployment and monitoring.&lt;br&gt;• ​Develops and enforces engineering standards, coding practices, and architectural guidelines across teams.&lt;br&gt;• ​Works closely with product, UX, and architecture teams to define scalable technical solutions.&lt;br&gt;• ​Mentors engineers at various levels and supports talent development through code reviews and knowledge sharing.&lt;br&gt;• ​Investigates production issues and leads root cause analysis and long-term solutions for system health.&lt;br&gt;• ​Champions innovation, system improvements, and performance optimizations across products and services. ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Complexity:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Leads projects with cross-functional dependencies and significant technical complexity. Guides technical strategy and drives execution. ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Required Supervision:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Functions independently and provides technical leadership to multiple engineers. Accountable for design decisions and engineering quality. ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Expertise:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Strong technical depth in system architecture, application development, and software design. Recognized for team leadership and reliable execution. ​ ​ ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;

QUALIFICATIONS:
&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• ​6–9 years of experience in software engineering&lt;br&gt;• ​Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field&lt;br&gt;• ​Proven experience leading development of distributed systems, cloud-native applications, or large-scale platforms&lt;br&gt;• ​Deep proficiency in programming languages, development frameworks, and cloud infrastructure (e.g., AWS, GCP, Kubernetes)&lt;br&gt;• ​Strong problem-solving, architecture design, and technical mentoring skills&lt;br&gt;• ​Excellent communication, collaboration, and leadership capabilities&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;hr&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Tekion is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, victim of violence or having a family member who is a victim of violence, the intersectionality of two or more protected categories, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information on our privacy practices, please refer to our Applicant Privacy Notice &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot; href=&quot;https://tekion.com/legal/privacy/applicant-and-candidate-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;re&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tekion:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Positively disrupting an industry that has not seen any innovation in over 50 years, Tekion has challenged the paradigm with the first and fastest cloud-native automotive platform that includes the revolutionary Automotive Retail Cloud (ARC) for retailers, Automotive Enterprise Cloud (AEC) for manufacturers and other large automotive enterprises and Automotive Partner Cloud (APC) for technology and industry partners. Tekion connects the entire spectrum of the automotive retail ecosystem through one seamless platform. The transformative platform uses cutting-edge technology, big data, machine learning, and AI to seamlessly bring together OEMs, retailers/dealers and consumers. With its highly configurable integration and greater customer engagement capabilities, Tekion is enabling the best automotive retail experiences ever. Tekion employs close to 3,000 people across North America, Asia and Europe.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Summary:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;​Drive the development and execution of product initiatives that enhance customer value and align with business objectives. Collaborate cross-functionally to deliver impactful product solutions, ensuring alignment with market needs and company goals. ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties &amp;amp;

RESPONSIBILITIES:
&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• ​Develop and execute product strategies and roadmaps for assigned product lines or features.&lt;br&gt;• ​Collaborate with engineering, design, marketing, and go-to-market teams to define and launch new features or products.&lt;br&gt;• ​Engage with customers, sales, and customer success teams to gather feedback, validate concepts, and ensure value delivery.&lt;br&gt;• ​Analyze market trends, competitive landscape, and usage data to inform prioritization and product evolution.&lt;br&gt;• ​Lead cross-functional initiatives, managing dependencies, risks, and communication across teams.&lt;br&gt;• ​Contribute to organizational frameworks, tools, and best practices.&lt;br&gt;• ​Define success metrics and ensure product outcomes are measurable and aligned to strategic objectives. ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Complexity:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Manages product areas with moderate complexity and cross-functional coordination. Leads initiatives from concept through launch and post-release optimization. ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Required Supervision:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Operates independently with guidance from senior leadership. Drives product direction and execution with moderate autonomy. ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Expertise:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Solid product management expertise with a strong understanding of user needs, market dynamics, and technical feasibility. ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;

QUALIFICATIONS:
&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• ​4–6 years of experience in product management, including ownership of product lines or features&lt;br&gt;• ​Background in Saa S, cloud platforms, or enterprise technology products&lt;br&gt;• ​Bachelor’s degree in Business, Computer Science, Engineering, or related field; advanced degree preferred&lt;br&gt;• ​Proven success in developing and scaling products in cross-functional environments&lt;br&gt;• ​Strong analytical, leadership, and communication skills&lt;br&gt;• ​Experience with Agile methodologies, product lifecycle tools, and data-driven decision-making&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;hr&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Tekion is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, victim of violence or having a family member who is a victim of violence, the intersectionality of two or more protected categories, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information on our privacy practices, please refer to our Applicant Privacy Notice &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot; href=&quot;https://tekion.com/legal/privacy/applicant-and-candidate-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;re&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tekion:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Positively disrupting an industry that has not seen any innovation in over 50 years, Tekion has challenged the paradigm with the first and fastest cloud-native automotive platform that includes the revolutionary Automotive Retail Cloud (ARC) for retailers, Automotive Enterprise Cloud (AEC) for manufacturers and other large automotive enterprises and Automotive Partner Cloud (APC) for technology and industry partners. Tekion connects the entire spectrum of the automotive retail ecosystem through one seamless platform. The transformative platform uses cutting-edge technology, big data, machine learning, and AI to seamlessly bring together OEMs, retailers/dealers and consumers. With its highly configurable integration and greater customer engagement capabilities, Tekion is enabling the best automotive retail experiences ever. Tekion employs close to 3,000 people across North America, Asia and Europe.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Summary:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;​The Security Engineer II is responsible for implementing and maintaining security controls, monitoring systems, and supporting incident response across the company’s technology environment. This role works on moderately complex projects with minimal supervision, ensuring that applications, infrastructure, and data remain secure and compliant. The Engineer II partners with IT, Engineering, and Security Operations to identify risks, remediate vulnerabilities, and strengthen overall security posture. ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties &amp;amp;

RESPONSIBILITIES:
&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• ​Implement, configure, and maintain security tools, monitoring systems, and access controls.&lt;br&gt;• ​Support vulnerability management, including scanning, analysis, and remediation coordination.&lt;br&gt;• ​Participate in incident detection, response, and root cause analysis.&lt;br&gt;• ​Collaborate with Engineering and IT teams to embed security best practices into development and infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;• ​Assist in maintaining compliance with security standards and regulatory requirements (e.g., SOC 2, ISO 27001, NIST).&lt;br&gt;• ​Perform security assessments and testing of applications, systems, and cloud environments.&lt;br&gt;• ​Contribute to threat modeling and risk assessments for new projects and technologies.&lt;br&gt;• ​Create and maintain security documentation, runbooks, and knowledge bases.&lt;br&gt;• ​Provide guidance and mentorship to junior engineers.&lt;br&gt;• ​Stay current on emerging security threats, tools, and technologies. ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;

QUALIFICATIONS:
&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• ​Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Engineering, or related field; equivalent experience considered.&lt;br&gt;• ​4–6 years of experience in security engineering, IT security, or related roles.&lt;br&gt;• ​Strong understanding of network, application, and cloud security principles.&lt;br&gt;• ​Experience with security tools such as SIEM, IDS/IPS, vulnerability scanners, and endpoint protection.&lt;br&gt;• ​Knowledge of cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, Azure) and security services.&lt;br&gt;• ​Familiarity with compliance and security frameworks (NIST, ISO 27001, SOC 2, CIS).&lt;br&gt;• ​Scripting or automation experience (Python, Bash, or equivalent) preferred.&lt;br&gt;• ​Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;br&gt;• ​Good written and verbal communication abilities.&lt;br&gt;• ​Industry certifications such as CISSP, GSEC, or CEH preferred.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;hr&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Tekion is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, victim of violence or having a family member who is a victim of violence, the intersectionality of two or more protected categories, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information on our privacy practices, please refer to our Applicant Privacy Notice &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot; href=&quot;https://tekion.com/legal/privacy/applicant-and-candidate-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;re&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tekion:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Positively disrupting an industry that has not seen any innovation in over 50 years, Tekion has challenged the paradigm with the first and fastest cloud-native automotive platform that includes the revolutionary Automotive Retail Cloud (ARC) for retailers, Automotive Enterprise Cloud (AEC) for manufacturers and other large automotive enterprises and Automotive Partner Cloud (APC) for technology and industry partners. Tekion connects the entire spectrum of the automotive retail ecosystem through one seamless platform. The transformative platform uses cutting-edge technology, big data, machine learning, and AI to seamlessly bring together OEMs, retailers/dealers and consumers. With its highly configurable integration and greater customer engagement capabilities, Tekion is enabling the best automotive retail experiences ever. Tekion employs close to 3,000 people across North America, Asia and Europe.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Provides strategic and operational leadership for multiple engineering teams. Oversees technical execution, cross-functional collaboration, and team development to ensure delivery of high-quality, scalable solutions aligned with Tekion’s business objectives.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties &amp;amp;

RESPONSIBILITIES:
&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Leads multiple engineering teams through the development lifecycle—from design through deployment—ensuring delivery of high-impact products and services.&lt;br&gt;• Collaborates with product, design, architecture, and operations leaders to define technical strategy and roadmaps.&lt;br&gt;• Oversees team structure, resource planning, hiring, and talent development across functional areas.&lt;br&gt;• Drives technical excellence by promoting engineering best practices, quality standards, and operational efficiency.&lt;br&gt;• Leads organizational transformation efforts related to scalability, automation, and platform modernization.&lt;br&gt;• Coaches engineering managers and senior engineers, providing mentorship, performance feedback, and career development support.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Complexity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Oversees engineering operations for multiple product domains or large-scale platforms. Leads strategic initiatives that influence both engineering practices and business outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Supervision:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Functions with broad autonomy. Aligns teams with company-wide objectives and works directly with senior and executive leadership.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recognized engineering leader with strong technical depth and people management experience. Known for scaling teams and systems in fast-paced environments.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;

QUALIFICATIONS:
&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• 10+ years of experience in software engineering, including 4+ years in engineering leadership roles&lt;br&gt;• Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related field&lt;br&gt;• Proven success in managing multiple engineering teams and delivering large-scale software solutions&lt;br&gt;• Deep understanding of cloud platforms, distributed systems, and development operations&lt;br&gt;• Strong strategic thinking, project management, and decision-making capabilities&lt;br&gt;• Excellent interpersonal, leadership, and communication skills&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;hr&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Tekion is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, victim of violence or having a family member who is a victim of violence, the intersectionality of two or more protected categories, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information on our privacy practices, please refer to our Applicant Privacy Notice &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot; href=&quot;https://tekion.com/legal/privacy/applicant-and-candidate-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;h&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;re&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Tekion:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;Positively disrupting an industry that has not seen any innovation in over 50 years, Tekion has challenged the paradigm with the first and fastest cloud-native automotive platform that includes the revolutionary Automotive Retail Cloud (ARC) for retailers, Automotive Enterprise Cloud (AEC) for manufacturers and other large automotive enterprises and Automotive Partner Cloud (APC) for technology and industry partners. Tekion connects the entire spectrum of the automotive retail ecosystem through one seamless platform. The transformative platform uses cutting-edge technology, big data, machine learning, and AI to seamlessly bring together OEMs, retailers/dealers and consumers. With its highly configurable integration and greater customer engagement capabilities, Tekion is enabling the best automotive retail experiences ever. Tekion employs close to 3,000 people across North America, Asia and Europe.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Summary:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Senior Product Designer leads the design of complex and high-impact features across Tekion’s platform, ensuring scalable, intuitive, and visually consistent user experiences. This role partners closely with Product, Engineering, and other cross-functional teams to define problems, explore solutions, and deliver elegant, user-centered designs. The ideal candidate demonstrates strong product vision, systems thinking, and mentorship capabilities. ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Duties &amp;amp;

RESPONSIBILITIES:
&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• ​Lead the design of complex product areas from discovery to delivery, including user research, flows, wireframes, high-fidelity UI, and prototypes&lt;br&gt;• ​Collaborate with stakeholders to define user problems, product strategy, and success metrics&lt;br&gt;• ​Facilitate and contribute to design critiques, cross-functional workshops, and ideation sessions&lt;br&gt;• ​Drive improvements to design systems, accessibility, and UX quality across the product&lt;br&gt;• ​Partner with developers to ensure accurate design implementation and iterate based on feedback&lt;br&gt;• ​Mentor junior designers and help uphold design best practices and team standards ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Job Complexity:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Leads design efforts on complex product initiatives with broad scope and strategic impact ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Required Supervision:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Operates independently and is trusted to lead critical projects with minimal oversight ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Expertise:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deep expertise in product design, UX research, and systems thinking; recognized for strategic insight and ability to influence product direction ​ ​&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;

